  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Business Angel Network onboarding</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project builds on the earlier PSD project PCB23PS02 which aimed to address the limited access to finance faced by early-stage (M)SMEs and young entrepreneurs in the Palestinian Territories by realizing a BAN network. This project focuses on the onboarding of the Angel Investor for the established Business Angel Network (BAN). A two-day bootcamp in Jordan, designed to introduce potential angel investors to the concept of early-stage investing and to provide them with some practical tools, knowledge, and connections to become active members of the network. The bootcamp also creates a space for regional exchange by involving experienced speakers and ecosystem partners from Jordan and Lebanon, fostering cross-border learning and collaboration.Through this approach, the project contributes to building a stronger investment culture in the Palestinian Territories. By linking entrepreneurs with engaged angel investors, it supports private sector growth, job creation, and more inclusive economic opportunities.</narrative>
  </description>
